A||N||6||rnoswal||Front nose piece||||1||
Z||000000||rnoswal||12-10-2000||11:09 PM||||Hi again, I own an 85 4 cyl and would like to put the front nose piece off an 87 on my car. Can I? Any modifications need to be done? What years interchange if any? Thanks.<P>Russ||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||12-10-2000||11:17 PM||||All Fiero bumper covers are interchangeable.  You can certainly put the later coupe ('87-'88) front fascia on your '85, but you will need the inner fender wells from the '87-'88 facia (and maybe the honeycomb absorber too).<p>[This message has been edited by mrfiero (edited 12-11-2000).]||||reg||10
Z||000002||sqoach||12-11-2000||01:34 AM||||trim would be different too i think. i'm pretty sure 84-86 coupes had the grooved molding and 87-88 coupes had smooth.<P>------------------<BR>sQoaCh<BR>fiero7@hotmail.com<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mysig_2.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Stoic||12-11-2000||08:21 AM||||yes, sqoach is right about the trim||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfiero||12-11-2000||03:01 PM||||Yes the trim is different, but it is only an aesthetical difference and won't interfere with the bumper fitting.  You can install an '87-'88 rear bumper cover and then replace all of the other ribbed trim with the smooth style pretty easily if you want.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||rnoswal||12-11-2000||08:22 PM||||Thanks!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||MrPBody||12-12-2000||11:05 PM||||I installed an '87 coupe front fascia on my '85 coupe.  it was fairly easy to do, and I like the way it looks; however, there were a few problems:<UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>The "waffle" impact absorber is different.  The '85 waffle is smaller, and may work under the '87 fascia.  I installed the '87 waffle.<BR>-<BR><LI>The '87 fascia has fatter cheeks; there is a gap between the fascia and '85 wheelwell liners.<BR>-<BR><LI>'85 turn signals don't align exactly with '87 fascia openings.  I think '87 turn signals mount about 1/2" lower.<BR>-<BR><LI>The fascia underside mounts to a curved spring steel (?) support attached to the bumper steel.  '85 and '87 fascias use different mounting holes, and the spring steel support is harder than my drill bits, so I'm going to try clamping the fascia in place.<BR>-<BR><LI>The '87 fascia uses different side marker lights.<BR>-<BR><LI>Of course, the '87 air dam and supports are different, as well as various panels and flexible shrouds that direct air to the radiator.<BR></UL><P>But it still looks good!<BR>||||reg||1
